2026-10-30T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2345) 'Every rendered video is one format: CineForm and FLAC in Matroska.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2345) 'The decider-pong recorders wrote H.264 and AAC in MP4. That is a lossy delivery format, and a second encode loses more.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2345) 'Check a video with `ffprobe`, which must report `cfhd`, `gbrp12le`, 1920x1080 and the `matroska` format.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2345) 'The format, how fast it encodes, and how a file is checked
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2345) 'Every rendered video is written as CineForm video and FLAC audio in a Matroska (`.mkv`) file. CineForm runs at `gbrp12le`, so RGB frames keep full chroma. MP4 is blocklisted as a container, and H.264 and AAC are not written as outputs. A tool that writes video refuses an output path that does not end in `.mkv`. Uncompressed PCM audio is accepted in place of FLAC (operator, 2026-10-23); both are lossless.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2345) '- RFD66606-2349, which replaces the encoder, the live recorder and the file check below. The format here stands.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

