2026-10-30T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2345) 'Why an intermediate
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2345) 'An intermediate must survive re-encoding and keep sharp synthetic edges.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2345) 'Encoder settings
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2345) 'The homebrew ffmpeg ships the `cfhd` encoder. It takes `yuv422p10le`, `gbrp12le` and `gbrap12le`. The recorders use `gbrp12le`, because their frames are RGB and Pong's edges are one colour against another. Audio is FLAC, or uncompressed PCM, at 48 kHz, stereo. An engine movie writer receives 32-bit samples, so it writes `pcm_s24le` and never 16-bit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2345) 'CineForm fails on a frame whose width is not divisible by 16 or whose height is not divisible by 8. A writer checks the size before it starts and refuses with a message that names the size, because the encoder otherwise dies mid-stream and the only symptom is a broken pipe.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2345) 'A live recorder pipes raw RGB to one ffmpeg process that writes CineForm in Matroska, then a second pass copies that video and adds the FLAC track. Nothing is held in memory past the pipe.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2345) 'Cost
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2345) 'On the Mac mini, `cfhd` encodes a 1080p test source at about 170 frames a second, so a 30 fps live render keeps up with room to spare. A file grows by about 20 MB a second at 1080p. A 2-minute render is about 2.4 GB and a 5-minute render about 6 GB. The Desktop filled to 43 GB in one session, so superseded renders are listed for deletion and deleted only on request.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2345) 'How a file is checked
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2345) '`ffprobe` must report `cfhd`, `gbrp12le`, 1920x1080, `flac` or a `pcm_s16le`/`pcm_s24le` stream at 48000 Hz and the `matroska` format, with the duration the run asked for. A frame is then pulled with `ffmpeg -ss` and looked at. That report and that frame are the check, whatever exit code the recorder returns.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2345) 'The guard and its control
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2345) '`recorder_second_opinion.py` exits with an error on any `--out` that does not end in `.mkv`. The planted control asked for `planted.mp4`: the run exited 1 and wrote no file.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2345) 'What changed in decider-pong
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2345) '`recorder_pong_v.py` and `recorder_second_opinion.py` now write CineForm and FLAC. Four superseded recorders that only wrote MP4 were deleted: `recorder_live.py`, `recorder_pong_live.py`, `recorder_pong_vector.py` and `recorder_realtime.py`. Every MP4 the session had made was removed and re-rendered.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2345) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2345  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-30T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2345) 'The workspace had no written format, so each recorder picked its own.
